{"actKind": "new", "audit": {"coverageKind": "newTaxa", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_parsley_zhao.y.l:0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/0:act", "kind": "act", "path": "0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_parsley_zhao.y.l", "subject": "balangicystis", "tree": "taxonomy"}
{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2006_parsley_zhao.y.l:0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/0:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/1/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2006_parsley_zhao.y.l", "subject": "balangicystis", "text": "Eocrinoid with ?five wedge-shaped basals above which in adult specimens\nat least six irregular circlets of polygonal plates with commonly five\nraised, flat-topped rays extend from plate center to plate angles.\nSutural pores between thecal plates absent. Ten or 15 brachioles in\nan essentially transversely elongated 2-1 -2 pattern across upper face\nof the theca. Brachioles longer than height of theca and robust\nrelative to thecal size. Tall cover plates present. Holdfast composed\nof short circlets of five or six platelets, some with prominent\ncircular boss. At least 40 holdfast circlets present in juvenile\nand adult specimens.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
